# --- Promotion determination ---

qa:AG18-QA-005-promotion
    a qa:PromotionDecision ;
    qa:finding qa:AG18-QA-005 ;
    qa:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAG-s21-collapse-dispatch-routing" ;
    qa:promoteToBranch "feature/pAG-s18-unify-envelope-handler" ;
    qa:rationale """Not a repeatable cross-branch pattern -- this is a single-owner doc-drift defect. Root cause is fully localized to AG.18's own commit 70cce097, which deleted SendRequestEnvelope::Compose/Acknowledge from crates/atm-core/src/protocol.rs without updating the paired ICD table/mapping it invalidated. Verified no later branch (AG.19, AG.20, AG.21) has touched docs/atm-daemon/protocol-icd.md at all since AG.18 (empty `git log develop..HEAD` for the file on each), so the stale text is unmodified drift, not a re-introduced or evolving pattern. Per sweep_scope ('feature/pAG-s18-unify-envelope-handler docs only') and the general rule that a docs-only fix stays on the branch that caused the divergence unless a later branch already touched the same lines, promote_to_branch is feature/pAG-s18-unify-envelope-handler, not the overall AG-ladder highest_open_branch (AG.21). Fix must merge-forward through AG.19/AG.20/AG.21 once applied.""" .
